$ gragas journal restore --help
--- exit 0
--- stdout

  Prints one line for each file the run changed: a cp of the
  copy it kept, or an rm for a file it made. It runs none of
  them, and it takes no --apply: you read the lines and
  paste
  them. For PowerShell or cmd it prints no line: it says
  each
  step in words, as rm and cp are not commands there. If a
  file
  no longer holds what the run left, it is refused and names
  the runs that changed it since.

    gragas journal restore <run>
    gragas journal restore <run> --json

  USAGE


    gragas journal restore <run> [--flags]


  FLAGS

    --accessible  Plain questions (ACCESSIBLE)
    --config      The settings file (GRAGAS_CONFIG)
    -h --help     Help for restore
    --json        Answer in one JSON document
    --no-color    No colour (NO_COLOR)
    --plain       Print plainly: nothing moves

--- stderr
